          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came into hospital because of low mood that had been getting worse over 6 weeks. You were also experiencing a loss of enjoyment in things, waking early in the morning, reduced appetite with around 4 kg of weight loss, and poor concentration. You were having thoughts of suicide, including thoughts of overdose. The team found you were having a depressive episode with active suicidal ideation. The team also noted recent relationship breakdown and work stress as triggers."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team assessed your thoughts of suicide carefully throughout your stay. By Day 3 these thoughts had become less intense. By Day 5 they were fleeting and passive, with no intent, and you were thinking about the future. No psychotic features were found.\n\nAn antidepressant (sertraline) was started on Day 3 (20/05). You were given psychoeducation. A safety plan was completed with you. You were seen by the liaison psychiatry team. On Day 5 the full team agreed you were ready to go home, with early follow-up arranged."
        },
        {
